Based on the coupon purchase policy document, here's the exact procedure for purchasing e-coupons for your study participants:

Exact Procedure for E-Coupon Purchase:
Step 1: Pre-Purchase Documentation (Section 2.2)
Prepare a project plan with the following information for Dean/Head of Department approval:

Project/activity: AI-Assisted L2 Poetry Writing Study
PI/department: Your name/department
Purpose/justification: Compensation for research participants (Sessions 2-3)
Budget availability, funding source and fund code: Specify your funding source (must be non-UGC funds)
Coupon details:
Type: E-coupon (specify vendor, e.g., gift card platform)
Value per coupon: (your amount, e.g., HK$100)
Quantity: (e.g., 10 participants)
Total value: (e.g., HK$1,000)
Timing and distribution plan: After Sessions 2-3 completion
Entitlement rules: Each participant receives one e-coupon upon study completion
Contact person and custodian: Your name
Step 2: Get Prior Approvals (Sections 2.1-2.3)
Confirm your funding source allows coupon purchases (non-UGC funds required)
Obtain approval from Dean/Head of Department or delegate
Ensure your ethics approval/research application clearly describes the coupon arrangement
Step 3: Submit Purchase Request (Section 2.4)
Do NOT purchase personally for reimbursement
Submit purchase request to Finance Office (FO) Procurement Team for centralized bulk buying
They will handle the actual purchase
Step 4: Secure Storage (Section 4.1)
Once received, store e-coupon codes in:

Secure, access-controlled systems
Use encryption where available
NOT in unencrypted spreadsheets, emails, or paper records
Log all access and transactions
Step 5: Distribution (Section 3)
Distribute only to eligible participants per approved plan
Use secure and verifiable delivery methods (encrypted email or secured platforms)
Maintain detailed distribution log (Annex 1 format):
Participant ID
Date of distribution
Coupon type and value
Serial number
Recipient acknowledgment
Step 6: Reporting (Section 5.1)
Record all expenditures in University financial system
Retain documentation for 7 years minimum
Report unused coupons to funding authority and FO for reconciliation
Key Prohibitions:
Cannot be reloadable or cash-withdrawal cards
Cannot be exchanged for cash
No returns accepted from participants
Next Action: Contact your Finance Office Procurement Team with the prepared project plan to initiate the purchase process.
